{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 12,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.707,
            0.05,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Geometric Twins"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.089,
            0.273,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": "We have,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.32,
            0.108,
            0.678,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "AO = OD (as O is the midpoint of AD)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.32,
            0.132,
            0.677,
            0.153
          ],
          "content": "BO = OC (as O is the midpoint of BC)."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.167,
            0.564,
            0.19
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Are there any other equal sides or angles?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.199,
            0.316,
            0.219
          ],
          "content": "We also have,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.24,
            0.23,
            0.757,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": "$\\angle AOB = \\angle DOC ,$ as they are vertically opposite angles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.258,
            0.847,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": "We see that the SAS condition (two sides and the included angle) is satisfied, and so we can conclude that the triangles are congruent."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.315,
            0.623,
            0.337
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "What are the Corresponding Vertices?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.342,
            0.848,
            0.42
          ],
          "content": "As we need AO and OD to overlap, and BO and CO to overlap for the triangles to exactly fit over each other, the corresponding vertices in ΔAOB and ΔDOC are A and D, O and O (vertex common to both the triangles), and B and C. Thus,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.426,
            0.429,
            0.572,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": "\\Delta  AOB  \\cong \\Delta  DOC .",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.458,
            0.847,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": "AB and DC are corresponding sides as they overlap when the triangles are superimposed. Thus, their lengths are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.507,
            0.316,
            0.53
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.534,
            0.846,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": "1. Identify whether the triangles below are congruent. What conditions did you use to establish their congruence? Express the congruence."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.221,
            0.576,
            0.443,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.566,
            0.583,
            0.779,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.808,
            0.848,
            0.887
          ],
          "content": "2. Given that CD and AB are parallel, and $\\mathrm{AB} = \\mathrm{CD}_{:}$ , what are the other equal parts in this figure? (**Hint:** When the lines are parallel, the alternate angles are equal. Are the two resulting triangles congruent? If so, express the congruence.)"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.812,
            0.934,
            0.839,
            0.951
          ],
          "content": "13"
        }
      ]
    }
